==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined by IBM researchers Barry Devlin and Paul Murphy in 1988.<ref>{{cite-journal|author=B. A. Devlin|title=An architecture for a business and information system|work=IBM Systems Journal|pages=60–80|year=1988|volume=27|issue=1|issn=0018-8670|doi=10.1147/sj.271.0060|author2=P. T. Murphy}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[collection]] of data, from a variety of [[source]]s, [[organized]] to provide useful [[guidance]] to an [[organization]]'s [[decision]]-[[maker]]s.
#: {{cot|en|data lake|data room}}

